@startuml data-source-switch
!theme plain
title PYQ data source — one env var decides where the data comes from (see docs/pyq/user-flows.md)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "web/ (Next.js)" {

  package "Screens — web/src/app" {
    component "/dashboard" as Dashboard
    component "/question-bank" as Bank
    component "/practice/{sessionId}" as Practice
    component "/revision, /reinforce,\n/bookmarks, /wrong-questions" as Revision
    component "/subscription" as Sub
  }

  package "Hooks — web/src/hooks/pyq" {
    component "index.ts\nuseTaxonomy, useAccess, useQuestions,\nuseStartSession, useAnswer, useSubmitSession,\nuseRevision, useStreak, useCollections …" as Hooks
    component "plans.ts\nusePlans, usePlanCheckout" as PlansHook
  }

  interface "PyqDataSource\nlib/data-source/types.ts" as Port

  package "lib/data-source" {
    component "index.ts\n(the switch)" as Switch
    component "mock-adapter.ts" as Mock
    component "api-adapter.ts" as Api
    component "kind.ts\nDATA_SOURCE_KIND" as Kind
  }

  component "data/mock + zustand stores" as MockData
  component "lib/api/client" as Client
  component "middleware.ts\n/api/* proxy" as Middleware
}

node "backend (NestJS)" {
  component "questions module\n/api/pyq/*, /api/admin/pyq/*" as Questions
  component "orders module\n/api/orders, /api/payments/verify,\n/api/webhooks/razorpay" as Orders
  database "Postgres\nschema pyq + public" as DB
}

Dashboard --> Hooks
Bank --> Hooks
Practice --> Hooks
Revision --> Hooks
Sub --> PlansHook
Sub --> Hooks

Hooks ..> Port : react-query wrappers\naround every call
PlansHook ..> Port

Port -- Switch
Kind --> Switch : NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_SOURCE\n"api" | anything else
Switch --> Mock : default
Switch --> Api : when "api"

Mock --> MockData : browser only, no backend
Api --> Client
Client --> Middleware : relative /api/* +\nbearer access token
Middleware --> Questions : BACKEND_API_URL
Middleware --> Orders
Questions --> DB
Orders --> DB

note right of Port
  The port is the only contract. Screens never import
  mock data or the API client — swapping data source is
  one env var and a rebuild, because Next inlines
  NEXT_PUBLIC_* at build time.

  Shapes on the port are the UI's, not the wire's; the
  api adapter translates, and maps 403
  PYQ_DAILY_LIMIT_REACHED to a DailyLimitError the hooks
  can show as an upgrade prompt.
end note

note bottom of Mock
  `capabilities` on the port tells screens what an
  adapter cannot do — free-text search and smart
  custom-test ordering are mock-only, and those
  controls are hidden in api mode.
end note

@enduml
